fin-art-b 2026-11-26: cracked.png (1 landing) and cracked2.png (2 landings) recreated to match the video: thin dark-brown
jagged crack lines on a transparent square (frames: i.ytimg.com/vi/aSc3Cs0eo7g/maxres1.jpg, maxres2.jpg, maxresdefault.jpg),
so they sit over light and dark squares alike; generated by a crack-path script (deterministic seeds), 512px. The old
cracked.png had the beige square and a legal-move dot baked in; broken.png (the thumbnail's falling rook) is gone: a broken
square is the plain black hole the video shows (sq-tint #0b0a09). Each square rotates the overlay by 90deg*(index%4).
